(7422657, 1171548, 69325, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by covenation:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m not making this a discussion but I did just cross reference 6 dictionary definitions and 2 of them stated "especially the face in some instances". But they all said "likeness of a person". But yes you were correct in that it could be any medium obviously...if you are correct then I''m certain the panel will boot it, no? In this case the photographer decided to display the likeness in obvious ways, and they did not incorporate the eyes... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>you''re both missing the big picture, and that is, she''s got a great ass!</td>', 'Originally posted by covenation: I''m not making this a discussion but I did just cross reference 6 dictionary definitions and 2 of them stated "especially the face in some instances". But they all said "likeness of a person". But yes you were correct in that it could be any medium obviously...if you are correct then I''m certain the panel will boot it, no? In this case the photographer decided to display the likeness in obvious ways, and they did not incorporate the eyes...   you''re both missing the big picture, and that is, she''s got a great ass!', '2015-12-16 15:26:37.000000', NULL, 0),
